1
00:00:13,395 --> 00:00:25,441
[SPEAKER_01]: The reason why a mind, a person, would still be dependent on the pleasure of the senses, despite knowing how little satisfaction they provide and so on, fundamentally, they don't really know where the problem is.

2
00:00:26,762 --> 00:00:38,127
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you know that the sense objects, the pleasures you get from them, are not satisfactory and so on, but you don't really understand the extent of the sense objects.

3
00:00:38,167 --> 00:00:41,369
[SPEAKER_01]: You don't really understand the extent of the pleasure you're chasing.

4
00:00:42,049 --> 00:00:50,534
[SPEAKER_01]: So, in other words, when you think about the dissatisfactory nature of the sense objects, that is not entirely accurate.

5
00:00:50,674 --> 00:00:57,918
[SPEAKER_01]: Because if it were entirely accurate, you would then also understand the peril of it, and you would lose any desire and zeal towards it.

6
00:00:59,078 --> 00:01:11,504
[SPEAKER_01]: So, the problem with people still being attracted to that which they know does not result in happiness, and it's actually doing them more harm than good.

7
00:01:11,624 --> 00:01:17,607
[SPEAKER_01]: The problem that people are still addicted to the pleasures of the senses, is they don't see where that pleasure begins.

8
00:01:18,688 --> 00:01:24,009
[SPEAKER_01]: They only see what they're used to seeing on the level of the sense objects.

9
00:01:24,549 --> 00:01:31,010
[SPEAKER_01]: But there is more to that picture, that it's left out, because of which the addiction is not uprooted.

10
00:01:31,790 --> 00:01:34,831
[SPEAKER_01]: And that which is left out is your own body.

11
00:01:35,531 --> 00:01:39,932
[SPEAKER_01]: It's pretty much the relationship of your own mind with your own body, of you with your own body.

12
00:01:40,592 --> 00:01:46,313
[SPEAKER_01]: So, when people get attracted to the sense objects, they don't realize that they have already accepted

13
00:01:47,858 --> 00:02:04,001
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's why the Buddha said, for as long as one's mind is not developed in regard to its own body, the desire towards sensuality will be there.

14
00:02:04,241 --> 00:02:04,442
[SPEAKER_01]: So,

15
00:02:09,952 --> 00:02:15,835
[SPEAKER_01]: There is the central pull towards sense objects, for the pleasure of it.

16
00:02:16,736 --> 00:02:25,160
[SPEAKER_01]: At the same time, your body, your senses, are there, peripherally, enduring, as a basis from which you are pressured.

17
00:02:26,282 --> 00:02:35,628
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it's the relationship on that peripheral level between you and that body that is pressuring you toward sense objects.

18
00:02:35,749 --> 00:02:37,169
[SPEAKER_01]: That's what needs to be understood.

19
00:02:38,250 --> 00:02:46,196
[SPEAKER_01]: And the reason why that's so hard to understand, or it takes a lot of effort to understand, is because the body, as a unity of your sense organs,

20
00:02:46,896 --> 00:02:50,358
[SPEAKER_01]: does not appear, cannot appear on the level of your sense objects.

21
00:02:50,758 --> 00:03:01,222
[SPEAKER_01]: So, your dependence on the pleasures of the sense objects is actually determined and dependent upon the pressure that your own body exerts on your mind.

22
00:03:02,423 --> 00:03:08,666
[SPEAKER_01]: So, that's the whole similes we gave in the past of, you know, taming an elephant or taming the bull.

23
00:03:08,946 --> 00:03:11,167
[SPEAKER_01]: It's like... it's a wild animal,

24
00:03:12,095 --> 00:03:25,885
[SPEAKER_01]: that you are tied to, inseparable from, your mind, and it wants to go left and right, and eat this, and not eat that, and avoid this, and it will pressure you until it gets what it wants.

25
00:03:27,146 --> 00:03:34,251
[SPEAKER_01]: So, the question is not about removing the agreeable and enticing things from the world to be free.

26
00:03:34,731 --> 00:03:39,455
[SPEAKER_01]: The question is about taming that which pressures you, because of which you're not free.

27
00:03:40,992 --> 00:03:50,696
[SPEAKER_01]: So, that's why a person is still attracted to the sense objects, despite knowing how little satisfaction sense objects provide, because that's... the knowledge is limited.

28
00:03:50,736 --> 00:04:07,363
[SPEAKER_01]: The knowledge of, oh, this is dissatisfactory, is pretty much only within the sense objects, failing to see this whole kind of underlying pressure of your own body, and the pleasure you depend on, on the level of the body, failing to see this wild animal underneath,

29
00:04:08,198 --> 00:04:09,819
[SPEAKER_01]: So, they don't see that as a problem.

30
00:04:09,879 --> 00:04:13,420
[SPEAKER_01]: They only think these sense objects that I remain...

31
00:04:13,500 --> 00:04:15,701
[SPEAKER_01]: I become obsessed about, that's where the problem is.

32
00:04:15,741 --> 00:04:22,783
[SPEAKER_01]: No, that's pretty much the end result of the problem already being there and fully controlling you.

33
00:04:23,803 --> 00:04:31,466
[SPEAKER_01]: So, that's why, yes, the sense restraint and not engaging with those sense objects that are inciting of lust and so on, is the prerequisite.

34
00:04:32,905 --> 00:04:43,036
[SPEAKER_01]: And then you get to see, really, the roots of the problem, which is pretty much the body, the senses, that crave the pleasure that they're used to.

35
00:04:43,196 --> 00:04:43,597
[SPEAKER_01]: That's it.

36
00:04:44,378 --> 00:04:49,963
[SPEAKER_01]: So, if you don't engage with the pleasures that you're used to, that used-to part will fade away.

37
00:04:51,064 --> 00:04:54,767
[SPEAKER_01]: The dependence on that will cease, because they haven't been engaging with it.

38
00:04:55,407 --> 00:05:01,972
[SPEAKER_01]: So, that's like the... if the animal is engaged in a perpetually wild behavior,

39
00:05:02,933 --> 00:05:06,975
[SPEAKER_01]: It's going to become used to that, and there will be its norm, there will be its measure, there will be its need.

40
00:05:07,636 --> 00:05:16,300
[SPEAKER_01]: But if then the animal is not allowed to engage with these sights, sounds, smells, tastes, touches that would be making its mind wild, and so on, it will calm down.

41
00:05:16,480 --> 00:05:26,205
[SPEAKER_01]: Whether it wants to calm down or not, it will calm down, because things that are of the agitating nature, things that are of the perturbing nature, are now

42
00:05:30,408 --> 00:05:55,141
[SPEAKER_01]: So, if you want to uproot the dependence on the pleasure of the sense objects, you pretty much have to uproot the dependence of the pleasure of this body, the agreeability, the ownership, the not seeing it peripherally as a thing that endures there on its own, with its own thirsts and hungers and perceptions and so on.

43
00:05:56,201 --> 00:06:04,163
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you need to fully disown the body, but that can only be done on the level of that correct peripheral recognition of what the body is.

44
00:06:04,763 --> 00:06:09,785
[SPEAKER_01]: It cannot be done on the level of observing the body with your senses, because, see, you're not observing the body.

45
00:06:10,185 --> 00:06:12,706
[SPEAKER_01]: You're observing the sense objects that require the body.

46
00:06:13,706 --> 00:06:21,448
[SPEAKER_01]: And even if you're, like, you know, catching every moment and every sensation that passes through the body, that's all on the level of sense objects.

47
00:06:22,705 --> 00:06:35,941
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's why none of that which is underneath it, which is that necessary requirement for perceiving the sense objects, none of that will be affected by that practice and by those efforts.

48
00:06:38,727 --> 00:06:52,416
[SPEAKER_01]: Again, in the same sense, an eye cannot see itself, and for as long as you believe that you can, you will be pretty much engaged in very futile attempts of accessing that which is inaccessible.

49
00:06:52,676 --> 00:06:54,957
[SPEAKER_01]: Accessing your senses on the level of sense objects.

50
00:06:56,058 --> 00:06:57,299
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's a contradiction in turn.

51
00:06:59,088 --> 00:07:17,690
[SPEAKER_01]: So, on the level of the body, on the level of the senses, so on the level of the framework of the world of the sense objects, fully purify the relationship between you and that body that appears peripherally, that's present peripherally, while you are engaged with sense objects, or when you're engaged with sense objects.

52
00:07:19,227 --> 00:07:33,910
[SPEAKER_01]: So, for as long as you have sight, eyes, nose, and so on, the world of the sense objects is there, and the body, as the unity of the sense organs, is peripheral to that.

53
00:07:35,171 --> 00:07:41,372
[SPEAKER_01]: It's always the background of that domain of the sense objects, and that's where you need to see it.

54
00:07:42,800 --> 00:07:47,985
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it's not about examining the individual organs and looking at it with other sense organs.

55
00:07:48,725 --> 00:07:50,807
[SPEAKER_01]: It's about understanding the sixth sense base.

56
00:07:51,608 --> 00:08:01,757
[SPEAKER_01]: It's understanding the body as that thing which is there, that needs to be tamed on the level of that peripheral, through not engaging with actual sense objects that are pulling you.

57
00:08:03,048 --> 00:08:07,473
[SPEAKER_01]: And then, that pressure that that body exerts over you will diminish.

58
00:08:08,133 --> 00:08:15,160
[SPEAKER_01]: And the clearer you see it on that level, that's revealed through sensory strain, by the way, the more you get used to it.

59
00:08:15,260 --> 00:08:17,823
[SPEAKER_01]: And the more you get used to it, the less pressure you will bear.

60
00:08:19,099 --> 00:08:39,228
[SPEAKER_01]: And then, the body will be seen correctly, and any possibility of the pleasure to be accessed, to be experienced through that body, will not be something that will interest your mind, because the mind would see the extent of danger, if it chooses to go down that rabbit hole.

61
00:08:39,328 --> 00:08:48,132
[SPEAKER_01]: So, the first, as I said, just to sum up basically, the first thing you want to do is, if you want to stop chasing the sense pleasures,

62
00:08:49,664 --> 00:09:11,434
[SPEAKER_01]: Start practicing mindfulness of the body correctly, not as an observation technique or watching sensations or modern vipassanas or whatever, but by seeing it peripherally as an enduring bag of skin that contains the sense organs that are attracted to the various pleasures that they get in their respective domains.

63
00:09:11,915 --> 00:09:12,535
[SPEAKER_01]: You want to learn

64
00:09:18,267 --> 00:09:30,170
[SPEAKER_01]: And you will get to see that, if you have been practicing sense restraints sufficiently, guarding of the sense doors sufficiently, being moderately eating, watchfulness, and dwelling in solitude.

65
00:09:31,210 --> 00:09:37,531
[SPEAKER_01]: Because company and the world, it pretty much requires your mind to be on the level of sense objects.

66
00:09:39,132 --> 00:09:43,933
[SPEAKER_01]: And if you have not been sufficiently withdrawn from that, you will not... you simply...

67
00:09:45,293 --> 00:09:47,214
[SPEAKER_01]: There isn't enough space, say.

68
00:09:50,347 --> 00:09:53,969
[SPEAKER_01]: as a thing that endures there in the world as a basis for all the sense objects and so on.

69
00:09:54,449 --> 00:09:59,552
[SPEAKER_01]: You will not be able to see the relationship between the two, and you will not be able to see the the right order between the two.

70
00:10:00,512 --> 00:10:18,782
[SPEAKER_01]: So, through sense restraint, moderation eating, and guarding of the sense doors, and dwelling in solitude, you get to discern the body as a thing on its own, in their bag of skin, with the sense organs, that have its own respective domains, that they're attracted to, repelled from, and so on.

71
00:10:19,932 --> 00:10:25,334
[SPEAKER_01]: And, eh... you will see then that the pleasure of the sense objects actually begins.

72
00:10:25,374 --> 00:10:30,416
[SPEAKER_01]: It's actually rooted and it remains on the level of that peripheral body and those sense organs.

73
00:10:30,936 --> 00:10:33,957
[SPEAKER_01]: They're the ones thirsting after and craving for and so on.

74
00:10:35,258 --> 00:10:44,541
[SPEAKER_01]: And, eh... now that you have been sufficiently withdrawn from it, eh... you can actually disown that whole pressure and the pull of these individual organs.

75
00:10:44,581 --> 00:10:49,263
[SPEAKER_01]: You can see them as individual, five individual animals that the Buddha gave the simile of.

76
00:10:50,453 --> 00:10:51,114
[SPEAKER_01]: You could see this.

77
00:10:51,194 --> 00:10:53,536
[SPEAKER_01]: Oh, these are the wild animals that need training.

78
00:10:54,037 --> 00:10:57,981
[SPEAKER_01]: When people are engaged and not withdrawn sufficiently from the sense objects, they can't.

79
00:10:58,021 --> 00:11:00,603
[SPEAKER_01]: They see that only in abstraction, which means they don't see it.

80
00:11:01,844 --> 00:11:12,375
[SPEAKER_01]: They don't see their organs as an independent entities that pretty much have its own life and cravings and needs that they need to tame and control.

81
00:11:13,792 --> 00:11:20,335
[SPEAKER_01]: So, each time there is a pull from the sight, sound, smell, taste, or touch, they are the ones pulled by sight, sound, smell, taste, or touch.

82
00:11:20,415 --> 00:11:29,598
[SPEAKER_01]: They don't see anything in between because those sense organs, those animals, do not appear on the level of sense objects that you're so used to looking at and measuring existence by.

83
00:11:30,279 --> 00:11:40,523
[SPEAKER_01]: So, that's why the whole practice of sense restraint and that correct mindfulness, that peripheral awareness we often talk about, it's that peripheral signs and features of that body that exists on the level

84
00:11:41,574 --> 00:11:46,638
[SPEAKER_01]: Around that which you're attending, at the background of it, that's what the body is.

85
00:11:46,778 --> 00:11:52,844
[SPEAKER_01]: That's the... that's what the Buddha meant by saying, knowing the body to the extent necessary for the final knowledge.

86
00:11:52,924 --> 00:11:54,305
[SPEAKER_01]: That's the measure of that extent.

87
00:11:55,065 --> 00:12:00,150
[SPEAKER_01]: How familiar with the phenomenon of the body you are, on the level of peripheral.

88
00:12:00,790 --> 00:12:15,483
[SPEAKER_01]: How steady your mind is in discerning the, you know, the presence of the body for what it is, on its own, without needing to attend to it directly, without needing to make it a sense object.

89
00:12:15,603 --> 00:12:22,890
[SPEAKER_01]: And if you develop that extent sufficiently, yeah, there will be no more... you will not be underlined

90
00:12:23,435 --> 00:12:26,376
[SPEAKER_01]: By lusting, craving and thirst of the individual senses.

91
00:12:26,817 --> 00:12:34,120
[SPEAKER_01]: By not seeing the senses, by being on the level of sense objects, that's how you are underlined by all the asavas, underlying tendencies.

92
00:12:34,961 --> 00:12:37,522
[SPEAKER_01]: They underline you because you go over them.

93
00:12:37,542 --> 00:12:42,064
[SPEAKER_01]: So, they become that which is under you, and it kind of directs you and pushes you and controls you.

94
00:12:42,805 --> 00:12:47,127
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you want to develop your mind to the extent necessary when you are not underlined, when you underline them.

95
00:12:47,900 --> 00:12:48,600
[SPEAKER_01]: Let's say like that.

96
00:12:49,101 --> 00:12:56,945
[SPEAKER_01]: That's in another sutra where it would have said that an arahant's mind is not overwhelmed by things, by dhammas, by pressures, by so on.

97
00:12:57,525 --> 00:12:58,906
[SPEAKER_01]: He is the one that overwhelms them.

98
00:12:59,286 --> 00:13:08,591
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's what it's meant by the order, establishing the right order, seeing what comes first, seeing the body on the level of the peripheral as that which is first, and not losing that context.

99
00:13:09,071 --> 00:13:13,593
[SPEAKER_01]: Despite of what comes on the individual basis of your attention, and so on.

100
00:13:14,514 --> 00:13:24,399
[SPEAKER_01]: So, whatever you're attending to, whatever pressure there is, desire for pleasure, and so on, the order of... that's determined by your knowledge now, does not change.

101
00:13:24,619 --> 00:13:28,341
[SPEAKER_01]: You still see that peripheral body as the necessary basis for all of this that's happening.

102
00:13:28,842 --> 00:13:37,586
[SPEAKER_01]: And all you need to do is, oh, if I protect the order, there will be no room to become underlined by perverting the order, by last aversion or distraction.

103
00:13:37,967 --> 00:13:38,547
[SPEAKER_01]: Practice that to

104
00:13:41,015 --> 00:13:47,399
[SPEAKER_01]: Lust, aversion and distraction will completely fade because they have not been maintained through the perversion of the order.

105
00:13:47,820 --> 00:13:52,843
[SPEAKER_01]: That's why ānanda said in that sutta that sensuality in itself is exactly perversion of the order.

106
00:13:54,132 --> 00:14:13,676
[SPEAKER_01]: Putting the sense object first, and everything else measured through that, as second, and not seeing the body peripherally, the necessary bases of sense organs peripherally, the sixth sense base peripherally, for what it is, to the extent that it is, as that which is first, the necessary container for everything else appealing or disagreeable in the world.

107
00:14:14,496 --> 00:14:16,817
[SPEAKER_01]: So, if you unpervert that perception,

108
00:14:17,833 --> 00:14:24,824
[SPEAKER_01]: There is absolutely no room for for lust to breed and expand and so on, or aversion or distraction.

109
00:14:25,986 --> 00:14:26,547
[SPEAKER_01]: So, that's it.

